# Writing Style

## Tone

- **Clear, contemporary, precise**
- Avoid inflated art jargon
- Avoid startup jargon unless explicitly needed
- Avoid vague claims like "explores the intersection of"
- Prefer **concrete language** about what the work stages, materializes, critiques, or ritualizes
- Make texts usable for museums, grant panels, residencies, and press

## When Possible

- Provide **short, medium, and long versions** (e.g., 30-word, 90-word, 150-word)
- Use **alt text** for all images
- Include **related tags** and internal links for discoverability

## Avoid

- Walls of text
- Engineering-job language
- Service pricing or consulting framing on art pages
- Startup / product pitch tone
- Generic portfolio language ("I do many things")
